  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Espejo de Tarapac&#xe1;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is an innovative and unique large scale power project which combines solar photovoltaic (PV) and pumped storage hydroelectricity (PSH) technology to provide clean renewable energy supply 24 hours a day, seven days a week. 

&#x2022; GCF is leading the first energy pumped storage hydroelectricity (PSH) technology in the Americas using natural topography, gravity and seawater, resulting in a 24/7 baseload combined solar photovoltaic (PV)/PSH solution.
&#x2022; The project will revitalize the economic livelihood of two Chilean villages of fishermen, allowing them to to diversify their businesses into the agricultural and tourism sectors with fresh running water to the community.
&#x2022; The project can be easily replicated in South America including Colombia, Mexico and Peru with similar topographies.</narrative>
  </description>
